  "statement": "A courier must leave city 1, visit every other city exactly once and come back to city 1. Travelling from city i to city j costs d[i][j]; the costs are not symmetric (d[i][j] may differ from d[j][i]). Find the cheapest tour.\nInput: the first line holds n (2 <= n <= 16). Each of the next n lines holds n integers: line i holds d[i][1] .. d[i][n] (d[i][i] = 0, otherwise 1 <= d[i][j] <= 1000000).\nOutput: a single integer, the cost of the cheapest tour.\nTrying every order of the cities is too slow for the largest tests.\n\nExample\nInput:\n4\n0 10 15 20\n5 0 9 10\n6 13 0 12\n8 8 9 0\nOutput:\n35\n(1 -> 2 -> 4 -> 3 -> 1 costs 10 + 10 + 9 + 6.)",
  "starter_code": "const data = require(\"fs\").readFileSync(0, \"utf8\").trim().split(/\\s+/).map(Number);\nconst n = data[0];\nconst d = [];\nfor (let i = 0; i < n; i++) d.push(data.slice(1 + i * n, 1 + (i + 1) * n));\n// Print the cost of the cheapest tour\n",
